{"units": [{"id": "mvp-comment-167-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: \"prefer to\" etc. The chorus does not understand this and asks for instruction, very fittingly, whereas this request would attach less well to the reproach."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-2-mentioned1", "translation": "wish"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ can be aorist like ⟦2⟧ (Kühner-Blass II, 462), but need not be;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-3-mentioned1", "translation": "to hear"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-3-mentioned2", "translation": "to do"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-4-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ of two endings ⟦2⟧. I.T. 1202 (cf. ⟦3⟧ 382) here because of the ambiguity of ⟦4⟧. But if ⟦5⟧, the sentence can also be taken as a maxim."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-4-mentioned1", "translation": "just"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-4-mentioned2", "translation": "perfect"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-4-mentioned3", "translation": "just things"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-4-mentioned4", "translation": "wish"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-5-comment1", "translation": "431 ⟦1⟧ neuter;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-5-mentioned1", "translation": "of the wise"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-6-comment1", "translation": "432 ⟦1⟧ should not prevail; before that ⟦2⟧ (fg) is better than ⟦3⟧. M: justice should prevail by itself, through clarification of the matter, while injustice seeks to cover itself with oaths."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-6-mentioned1", "translation": "not to prevail"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-6-mentioned2", "translation": "the just things"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-6-mentioned3", "translation": "the unjust things"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-7-comment1", "translation": "With ⟦1⟧ 433 the questioning of the accused is also permitted;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-7-mentioned1", "translation": "question"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-8-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ has nothing to do with Attic ⟦2⟧ as the opposite of ⟦3⟧, but rather to ⟦4⟧ the opposite is ⟦5⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-8-mentioned1", "translation": "straight justice"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-8-mentioned2", "translation": "straight justice"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-8-mentioned3", "translation": "counter-plea"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-8-mentioned4", "translation": "straight"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-167-8-mentioned5", "translation": "crooked"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-168-1-comment1", "translation": "434 ⟦1⟧ —: so you are ready for this too?"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-168-1-mentioned1", "translation": "or even"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-169-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ = ⟦2⟧, as (Weckl.) ⟦3⟧ ⟦4⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-169-1-mentioned1", "translation": "turn upon me"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-169-1-mentioned2", "translation": "entrust to me"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-169-1-quote1", "translation": "nor turn upon others"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-comment1", "translation": "435 ⟦1⟧ is always \"corresponding\", 271. ⟦2⟧. ⟦3⟧. ⟦4⟧; but the genitive cannot be explained (although the scholiast also had it: ⟦5⟧ (scil.) ⟦6⟧), and one can easily emend with Hermann: ⟦7⟧, to repay your friendly reception with what is fitting (thus ⟦8⟧ = ⟦9⟧). Cf. ⟦10⟧ ⟦11⟧. 1318. ⟦12⟧. 312. ⟦13⟧. Whether ⟦14⟧ with M, or ⟦15⟧, which lies in the reading of fg, is hard to decide; ⟦16⟧v is easily supplied from ⟦17⟧ to the optative ⟦18⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-mentioned1", "translation": "worthy"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-mentioned2", "translation": "of worthy things"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-mentioned3", "translation": "being of parents"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-mentioned4", "translation": "worthy things in return for worthy things"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-mentioned5", "translation": "worthy things"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-mentioned6", "translation": "worthy reverence"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-mentioned7", "translation": "revering"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-mentioned8", "translation": "we would revere"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-mentioned9", "translation": "which"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-mentioned10", "translation": "would turn"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-mentioned11", "translation": "we would revere"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-170-1-quote1", "translation": "this reproach comes in return for reproach"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: as at 198."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-1-mentioned1", "translation": "in turn"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ the matricide or whatever it is you have done; ⟦2⟧. seek to justify yourself."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-2-mentioned1", "translation": "misfortunes"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-2-mentioned2", "translation": "then etc."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ (so, not -⟦2⟧ as Ddf.) cannot be aorist, any more than most of the other forms in -⟦3⟧ Kühner-Blass II, 178f. In A. cf. ⟦4⟧ 566, ⟦5⟧ 857 etc. (this aoristic). V. 440"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-3-mentioned1", "translation": "defend yourself"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-3-mentioned2", "translation": "put"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-3-mentioned3", "translation": "to place"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-3-mentioned4", "translation": "you accomplished"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-3-mentioned5", "translation": "to hold"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-4-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: to the ⟦2⟧ fled the ⟦3⟧, ⟦4⟧. ⟦5⟧. ⟦6⟧; at Apollo's as at Athena's the eternal fire was the symbol of this hearth, ⟦7⟧. ⟦8⟧ (lamp of Callimachus at the old cult image of Athena). ⟦9⟧ (M) is not to be adopted, because this form is used only under metrical compulsion, as at 311, Ddf."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-4-mentioned1", "translation": "of the hearth"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-4-mentioned2", "translation": "hearth"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-4-mentioned3", "translation": "suppliant"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-4-mentioned4", "translation": "our"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-5-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: cf. 92 ⟦2⟧, 151 ⟦3⟧;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-5-mentioned1", "translation": "reverend"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-5-mentioned2", "translation": "reverence"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-5-mentioned3", "translation": "revering"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-6-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ like ⟦2⟧ ⟦3⟧; on Ixion, the prototype of those seeking refuge because of murder, see below on 717f."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-6-mentioned1", "translation": "suppliant"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-171-6-mentioned2", "translation": "I will approach as suppliant"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-173-1-comment1", "translation": "443 f. ⟦1⟧ would be in nom.-acc. ⟦2⟧. —"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-173-1-mentioned1", "translation": "of the last of your words"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-173-1-mentioned2", "translation": "the last of your words"}]}